Context: section (VII), 'Calculs dans Sl(2,Ẑ)/±1', from the Longue Marche continuation on the 'équation des lacets'. ρ is the order-3 element of PSL(2,Z) acting by conjugation, with ρ(g)=ρgρ^{-1} and ρ^2(g)=ρ^{-1}gρ. Grothendieck tests the 3-cycle cocycle relation g·ρ(g)·ρ^2(g)=1, relation (79). This relation is one of the defining relations of the Grothendieck–Teichmüller-type 'lacets' equations. He tests it on the image of g=(a b; c d) in GL(2,Ẑ) modulo ±1.

On this page:
(1) He computes gρ(g)=(P Q; R S) explicitly, relation (81):
- P=(a+b)(c+d−b);
- Q=−a(c−b)−bc=δ−a(c+d−b);
- R=(c+d)^2−d(a+b)=(c+d)(c+d−b)−δ;
- S=ad−c(c+d)=δ−c(c+d−b);
- here δ=ad−bc=det g.
(2) Modulo ±1, the equation reads gρ(g)=±ρ^2(g^{-1}). Since ρ(−g)=−ρ(g), the substitution g→−g swaps the signs. So one reduces to the + sign, equation (82): gρ(g)=ρ^{-1}(g^{-1}).
(3) By (77), ρ^2(g^{-1})=δ^{-1}(a+b, c+d−a−b; b, d−b). He then works factor by factor in ∏_ℓ SL(2,Z_ℓ), so in an integral domain. The P-entry gives (a+b)(c+d−b)=(a+b)/δ. Hence either a+b=0 or c+d−b=1/δ.
(4) Case 1, a+b≠0, so c+d−b=1/δ, relation (83). The remaining entries Q=(c+d−a−b)/δ=1/δ^2−a/δ, R=b/δ and S=(d−b)/δ=1/δ^2−c/δ each reduce to the single condition δ^3=1, relation (84). The margin notes this condition is evidently necessary a priori: take determinants of g·ρ(g)·ρ^2(g)=1.
(5) Case 2, a=−b. Then g=(−b b; c d) and δ=−b(c+d), so d=−δ/b−c. This gives P=0, Q=−b^2, R=δ^2/b^2 and S=δ+c(δ/b+b). The case is finished on the next page: b^3=δ^3=1, plus a linear condition on c.

This is an explicit determination of the solutions of the 3-cycle relation in a small, computable quotient (PSL/PGL(2,Ẑ)). Grothendieck himself flags it as 'par acquit de conscience'.
